      "created_at": "2014-07-02T23:24:25.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Just a quick question.... This occured in a game we played earlier and would like some clarification if possible...</p><p>It was 4 players (Legacy, Unity, Bunker, The Sentinels). Legacy had 4 cards in play. I was playing The Sentinels who had about 8 cards in play. Unity and Bunker had about 3 i think (but definitely less than Legacy).</p><p>Then Citizen Dawn drew this card.</p><p>Citizen Summer: At the end of the villain turn, this card deals the 2 heroes with the most cards in play 3 fire damage each.</p><p>So how does the damage work in this case? Is it...</p><p>1) All 4 members of The Sentinels take 3 damage, then Legacy takes 3 damage.</p><p>2) Two members of The Sentinels take 3 damage. No one else takes any damage.</p><p>3) I get to choose one member of The Sentinels to take 3 damage. Legacy takes 3 damage.</p><p>I'm not exactly sure what the ruling would be in this case, but we went with option 3 after some debate on rule interpretation.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:41:45.300Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
